  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Cocoa producers by innovative cocoa fruit chains</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">It should be applauded that many chocolate manufacturers acknowledge the responsibility they hold in alleviating farmer poverty. If the industry is serious about living incomes, pathways should be developed which go beyond traditional supply chain practices, focusing instead on creating local value.This project would like to create extra income for cocoa farmers by adding value via cocoa juice. Cocoa juice is a refreshing fruity drink made from the pulp of the cocoa pod, a product which usually goes to waste. Importantly, the beans of the cocoa pod can be converted to high-quality chocolate, even after cocoa juice has been extracted. This innovation offers cocoa farmers and their households the opportunity to valorise part of their commodity that was previously wasted.  This project has the following objectives:&#xb7;	To establish a cocoa juice chain in Ivory Coast.&#xb7;	Increase the sustainability of the cocoa chain by producing extra value out of fruit and investing in climate smart production and agroforestry.&#xb7;	Extra jobs for youth, especially women.&#xb7;	Traceable sourcing for extra transparency and more impact communication to customers.&#xb7;	Create extra markets for the cocoa juice and develop an extra Ivorian supply chain to provide cocoa juice for Kumasi Drinks.</narrative>
  </description>
